    "chunk_text": "[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc1\u0dc4\u0d9a\u0dca\u0da7\u0d9a \u0d85\u0da7\u0dd2\u0db4\u0dd4\u0dc4\u0daf\u0db8\u0dd2 \u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dad\u0daf]\n\n202] \u0dc1\u0dca\u0ddc\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0dd0 \u0db3\u0d9a 17\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf \u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0dca \u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) The next speaker is the Hon. Tharaka Balasuriya. You have 10 minutes.\n\nSir, I think it is bit of a truncated Judgment and I am also baffled by it since the Constitution states that Parliament has control over public finance. However, I am not in any way saying that the people who have filed the cases have no right to file those and of course, the learned Supreme Court Judges have their own right to express their opinion. But, I feel this is not the right time - I am only looking at it from a political angle - for such a Judgment as it would only divide the country. And also to decide that only one person or a certain number of persons are responsible, the actions they had taken are arbitrary and those aggravated the economic situation, I do not think is a very fair Judgment. We know that there are root causes for this. The COVID-19 pandemic was one of the root causes. Also, there have been other countries which have become bankrupt due to certain policies implemented at that time, including the Modern Monetary Theory. That was implemented not only in Sri Lanka, but in other countries, too. So, to decide that the decisions and policies which were carried out at that time are arbitrary, I do not think is a fair Judgment. It is a 300-page Judgment and I have not read the entirety of it. The Court also went on to hold, I quote from the Judgment:\n\n\u201c\u2026 that administrative acts and decisions contrary to \u2018public trust\u2019 would be in excess and/or abuse of power by the Executive and therefore, violative of the fundamental rights in general and Article 12(1) of the Constitution in particular, which guarantees equality before the law and equal protection of the law.\u201d\n\nThe administrative acts and decisions, Sir, are the policy decisions. The administrative acts are policy decisions put into action and that is a right of the Executive."
  },
