    "description": "Hansard of November 20, 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1702029688030357.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2023-11-20-2023-11-20-0123",
    "chunk_index": 123,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "b125c76c68e7107098fae8c26ffb2c69",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "stake and the law of the jungle took precedence in the first half of the year 2022. We all are aware that under those circumstances, there was no investment flow into this country and the national economy was affected, tourist arrivals halted and as a result, people had to undergo difficulties they had not experienced earlier.\n\nThis Budget was presented under that background and it is not an easy task. We can overcome these challenges only by embracing new concepts and following the path of development, which might not be popular to the people, but is certainly sustainable.\n\nThe era of politics based on fairy tales is now over; a country cannot be developed by making false promises. We need to follow correct economic policies and make a hard struggle to overcome the present situation. The Budget presented by the Minister of Finance reflects that principle. Sri Lanka\u2019s situation is now better than it was before, a year ago. I do not say that the economy has completely recovered, but it has become comparatively better. We can certainly create a more favourable economic environment in the near future, if we adopt correct economic policies without adhering to short-term popular measures.\n\nThis Budget has addressed the low-income earners\u2019 requirements and for the \"Aswesuma\" programme, it has allocated Rs. 188 billion, which is around three times the present allocation.\n\nFor the salary incentives of the public servants and pensioners, an additional sum of Rs. 133 billion has been allocated.\n\nAlso, an additional Rs. 5,000 million has been allocated to increase the monthly allowances for senior citizens, the disabled, kidney patients et cetera.\n\nDue to the COVID situation and the economic crisis, no allocations were made for the Decentralized Budget for the last two years. This year, a sum of Rs. 11,250 million has been allocated for the Decentralized Budget, which will help enhance rural development and provide necessities for the villagers."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2023-11-20-2023-11-20",
    "num": "2023-11-20",
    "date_str": "2023-11-20",
    "description": "Hansard of November 20, 2023",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1702029688030357.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2023-11-20-2023-11-20-0124",
    "chunk_index": 124,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "6f8a39664fb10307ad475b093d603dc7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2064,
    "chunk_text": "Due to the COVID situation and the economic crisis, no allocations were made for the Decentralized Budget for the last two years. This year, a sum of Rs. 11,250 million has been allocated for the Decentralized Budget, which will help enhance rural development and provide necessities for the villagers.\n\n1223 1224\n\n[ \u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d85\u0db1\u0dd4\u0dbb \u0dd2 \u0dc3\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0dd9\u0dd9\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0d9a\u0db1\u0dc0\u0dbb\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 2]\n\nmakes me most happy is the relief given to the people despite the trying times we are faced with.\n\nThe increase in the cost of living allowance of public servants by Rs. 10,000 per month and that of the pensioners by Rs. 2,500 per month will be welcomed by all. The Government has appealed to the private sector to follow suit and increase their workers' salaries as well. We hope that the private sector will rise to the occasion.\n\nWhile addressing the needs of the poorer sections of the society, President Ranil Wickremesinghe has not failed to make several other Proposals taking into consideration the long-term needs of the country and its economic development. The list of such Proposals is too long to bear repetition, having regard to the limited time given to me. However, a few important ones deserve mention.\n\nIn perusing the Budget Proposals, I find that despite the economic restraints, a colossal sum of money has been allocated for education, health and agriculture. Several important reforms in the field of education outlined by the President will give a boost to the growth of the economy in the long run. The setting up of a National Council on Higher Education, the National Higher Education Commission and the National Skills Commission together with the expansion of science and technology education in the universities give hope to the younger generation.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8 \u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, you have only two more minutes."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
