    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1702029688030357.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2023-11-20-2023-11-20-0125",
    "chunk_index": 125,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "144c895c08f14740e45059dcfd49adef",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1868,
    "chunk_text": "In perusing the Budget Proposals, I find that despite the economic restraints, a colossal sum of money has been allocated for education, health and agriculture. Several important reforms in the field of education outlined by the President will give a boost to the growth of the economy in the long run. The setting up of a National Council on Higher Education, the National Higher Education Commission and the National Skills Commission together with the expansion of science and technology education in the universities give hope to the younger generation.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8 \u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, you have only two more minutes.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0d92.\u0d91\u0da0\u0dd2.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0dc6\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b8f.\u0b8e\u0b9a\u0bcd.\u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bcc\u0bb8\u0bbf) (The Hon. A.H.M. Fowzie) Then, give me a few more minutes, Madam.\n\nThe Proposal to establish four new universities in different parts of the country is certainly a step in the right direction. The Proposal to develop State universities while opening up non-State universities will provide further opportunities for those who are interested in pursuing higher education within the country. The \u201cEnglish for all\u201d Proposal, which aims to provide English literacy to all by 2034, will help the youth to access employment opportunities both here and abroad.\n\nThe health sector in the country has been facing numerous challenges in recent times. The hardest hit are\n\nthe poor who rely heavily on the public health sector for their health needs. It is, therefore, most welcome that the President has paid attention to the needs of this sector with several proposals which will help improve the situation."
  },
