    "md5": "58df8038c04470c4cd014a31718b53b4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2017,
    "chunk_text": "The need of the country will have to be put first before any political will. It shows why such a project is required, why we need to spend so much money on a project of that nature. So, Sir, I urge the Government at this moment in time not to delay that. Look at this Bill as a Bill of national importance and bring it to Parliament as early as possible. The Leader of the Opposition, the Hon. Sajith Premadasa, has also pledged his support for such a Bill. So, I think this Bill could be passed in Parliament with a majority, certainly, with two-thirds of the Members of Parliament agreeing to it. We really do\n\n1297 1298\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nrequire this Bill, that I cannot stop stressing the need for such a Bill.\n\nNow, we are going ahead with the Budget process. Tomorrow, this House will vote on the Second Reading of the Appropriation Bill, 2024. So, with that in mind, I think this Government has a golden opportunity to bring in the National Evaluation Bill to Parliament. Both sides of the aisle can agree upon it, debate, bring in amendments and pass the Bill, which, in God\u2019s name, is useful for this country so that when this Parliament is dissolved in the next few months or maybe, at the end of 2024, the people of this country will, at least, say that this Parliament did pass another Bill fundamentally required for this country's future.\n\nHon. Presiding Member, as you know, the professionals and their kids are leaving this country as never before simply because they do not see a future in this country. But, if we have an Act for evaluation, every cent spent by this Government and by future governments would be evaluated and there would be transparency and accountability to the people of this country as to how their hard-earned money collected as tax has been spent. Sir, I do not wish to speak any further. I wish the Hon. Shehan Semasinghe and the Government every success in terms of bringing in that Bill. Please bring it in as soon as possible and we will support it."
  },
