    "chunk_size_bytes": 1898,
    "chunk_text": "[12.49 p.m.] \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d91\u0dda.\u0d92. \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dad\u0dd2\u0dbb\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b8e\u0bae\u0bcd.\u0b8f. \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bae\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd) (The Hon. M.A. Sumanthiran) Thank you, Hon. Presiding Member, for the time allotted to speak a few words on these Heads of expenditure. We have had an interesting Debate so far with the Hon. President also participating in it.\n\nAnd what has that resulted in? The President has been saying from the time he took over as Prime Minister and then, as President that he will resolve the Tamil national question. He had three All-party Conferences, one last year and two this year, for that very purpose. But, he or even this House is unable to resolve this one issue. This is a no-brainer. You keep us out of the Constitutional Council and then you talk about resolving the Tamil national question in a just manner. How can you do that? You cannot even fill that vacancy. This matter had come into sharp focus a few days ago. There\n\n87 88\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dba) \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0dc3\u0dd2\u0dbd\u0dd3\u0db8 \u0daf\u0dda\u0db8\u0da2\u0dba\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2023 \u0daf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dd9\u0dd0\u0dda\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd 22\n\nis a deadlock situation in the Constitutional Council - everybody knows about that - when one seat is still vacant. If that had been filled, there would not have been a deadlock. So, the country must know that while you all wax eloquent saying all are equal, everyone in the country will have representation, in a body like the Constitutional Council, which is a very important body, you still deprive us of a place. And, how can you face anyone and claim this is governance in the right way? So, today, I am raising this as a serious issue, not just as filling of a vacancy in the Constitutional Council, but as a serious national issue. Our complaint for several decades has been that we have been left out of the national life of this country."
  },
