    "chunk_size_bytes": 1636,
    "chunk_text": "is a deadlock situation in the Constitutional Council - everybody knows about that - when one seat is still vacant. If that had been filled, there would not have been a deadlock. So, the country must know that while you all wax eloquent saying all are equal, everyone in the country will have representation, in a body like the Constitutional Council, which is a very important body, you still deprive us of a place. And, how can you face anyone and claim this is governance in the right way? So, today, I am raising this as a serious issue, not just as filling of a vacancy in the Constitutional Council, but as a serious national issue. Our complaint for several decades has been that we have been left out of the national life of this country.\n\nThis week is an important week. This is a week in which we honour the dead, who fought for us. I am not hesitant to say it in that way. Why did they fight for us? Because we were thrown out of the national life. There was no other way for us. Things went wrong and we are not in that mode anymore. We have expressly said, we are willing to live within one, united, undivided and indivisible country. We are yet willing to. But then, how is that being reciprocated? It is up to you; you have to decide. You cannot just sing us along all the time. And it is important while the relatives and others in the North and the East remember their dead that I say this in this House: do not take us for granted. The superior number does not make you right. Superior numbers often make you wrong, because you think you can bulldoze your way with your numbers. That is what you do in this House also."
