    "chunk_size_bytes": 2227,
    "chunk_text": "\u0b85\u0ba4\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb1\u0b95\u0bc1, \u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bae\u0bcd\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0bbf. \u0b9a\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bc8\u0bb5\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4 \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd \u0b85\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9a\u0ba9\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0bb1\u0bc1 \u0b85\u0b95\u0bc8\u0baa\u0bb5, \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd [\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b85\u0b9c\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b9c\u0baa\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bb7] \u0ba4\u0bae\u0bc8\u0bae\u0bae \u0bb5\u0b95\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd.\n\nWhereupon THE HON. PREMNATH C. DOLAWATTE left the Chair, and THE DEPUTY SPEAKER [THE HON. AJITH RAJAPAKSE] took the Chair.\n\nThere were so many other matters raised during this Discussion, especially the matters raised by the Hon. M.A. Sumanthiran, President\u2019s Counsel. He was very critical about the speech made by the Hon. President in Parliament today. During 2015 to 2019, when the Hon. Ranil Wickremesinghe was Prime Minister, everything he did was admired and praised by the Hon. Sumanthiran. But, when he could not get the Hon. Ranil Wickremesinghe on the track he expected him to be, he has become serious and a critic of the President's actions. Anyway, Hon. Member, that is your right in this democratic country.\n\nHon. Sumanthiran, you were making some allegations or complaints about appointments to the Constitutional Council. As you are aware, when we enacted the Ninteenth Amendment to the Constitution on 28th April, 2015, we ensured that the Constitutional Council shall be represented by all communities, that all the pluralistic features of the society would be taken into consideration and that there would be no lacuna; we ensured that the\n\nrights of every community are guaranteed through all these processes. Thereafter, unfortunately, as you said, there was an intervention with the Twentieth Amendment to the Constitution. But, I think within a period of one year, we were able to reverse it; you all supported us and we introduce the Twenty First Amendment to the Constitution. That was passed with 179 votes and one against. In that also, we ensured that when members are appointed to the Constitutional Council, all the political parties in Parliament are well-represented.\n\nThen, I would like to draw your attention to Article 41A. (1)(f) of the Constitution. It states, I quote:"
  },
