    "md5": "0ec3fc7a095c28f1cc39b96c7283fc88",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1953,
    "chunk_text": "rights of every community are guaranteed through all these processes. Thereafter, unfortunately, as you said, there was an intervention with the Twentieth Amendment to the Constitution. But, I think within a period of one year, we were able to reverse it; you all supported us and we introduce the Twenty First Amendment to the Constitution. That was passed with 179 votes and one against. In that also, we ensured that when members are appointed to the Constitutional Council, all the political parties in Parliament are well-represented.\n\nThen, I would like to draw your attention to Article 41A. (1)(f) of the Constitution. It states, I quote:\n\nThen, the general criterion is given in Article 41A. (4) thereof, which states, I quote:\n\n\u201cin nominating the five persons referred to in sub-paragraph (e) of paragraph (1), the Prime Minister, the Speaker and the Leader of the Opposition or the Members of Parliament, as the case may be, shall ensure that the Council reflects the pluralistic character of Sri Lankan society, including professional and social diversity.\u201d\n\nTherefore, the constitutional provision that all the persons are treated equally and all the communities are well-represented is ensured without any failure not only in Parliament, but in the Constitutional Council, too. Then, there are similar provisions when it comes to independent Commissions also; in appointment of members for every Commission, similar provisions are provided in the Constitution.\n\nNow, the appointment under the Article 41A. (1)(f) of the Constitution is the issue.\n\nWith regard to that, I must draw your attention, Hon. Chairman - I think you must bring this to the notice of the Hon. Speaker as well - to Article 41A.(3), which states, I quote:\n\n\u201cIt shall be the duty of the Speaker to ensure that nominations for appointments under sub-paragraph (e) or sub-paragraph (f) of paragraph (1) are made, whenever an occasion for such nomination arises.\u201d"
  },
