    "chunk_size_bytes": 998,
    "chunk_text": "who spent his entire political life selling the interests of the Tamil people in return for the crumbs that fell off the majoritarian head table, I take this opportunity to bow my head to the great heroes who sacrificed their lives so that the Tamil people could live with their rights and achieve their aspirations, at least, for future generations.\n\nHis Vote is also being discussed at this Committee Stage Discussion. I think these are all signs of times to come, Sir. It is a slippery slope that he has stepped on to and he is slipping down very fast. It is unfortunate because no one doubts the experience President Wickremesinge has. He could have, in fact, served this\n\ncountry in a legitimate way by allowing an election, calling for an election, having the people elect a Parliament which they could then say is representative and through that process, maybe, if he had an opportunity to play a leading role, then, certainly, he would be credible. Unfortunately, he chose a different path."
