    "chunk_size_bytes": 2029,
    "chunk_text": "country in a legitimate way by allowing an election, calling for an election, having the people elect a Parliament which they could then say is representative and through that process, maybe, if he had an opportunity to play a leading role, then, certainly, he would be credible. Unfortunately, he chose a different path.\n\nThis year, Sir, the Hon. Selvarajah Kajendren of our party, who is seated next to me, was taking part in a protest in Thaiyiddy against an illegal viharaya that has been built on a private land. When he was protesting, the police came and surrounded him. They did not arrest him, but he was under siege like what is happening in Gaza. He is a diabetic. So, when food was brought to him so that he could maintain his sugar levels, the police arrested the person who brought food, Theepan Thileeshan, who is our organizer for the Jaffna District.\n\nThen, his lawyer, Mr. Kanagaratnam Sugash, came to the site, introduced himself as the lawyer and wanted to speak to the Hon. Selvarajah Kajendren to find out what the situation was. He, too, was arrested despite the fact that he identified himself as a lawyer. Several others,\n\n137 138\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dd9\n\nsome members of the public, who tried to intervene were arrested as well. In total, over eight persons were arrested. We, subsequently, went and made complaints to the Human Rights Commission with regard to that incident. Whilst this incident was going on and illegal arrests were taking place, we had made complaints to the Human Rights Commission and the person in charge of the Commission in Jaffna visited the vicinity. When he was visiting the place and taking notes, he was threatened and was filmed. When he objected thereafter, he was almost manhandled. Then, he left the vicinity. Subsequently, the police had complained to the Human Rights Commission and the file with regard to the incident that was being investigated by the Commission has now been transferred to Colombo and nothing has happened. Nothing has happened!"
