    "chunk_text": "I was just looking at the Recurrent Expenditure for defence. It is an exorbitant amount! Last year, Verit\u00e9 Research has carried out a research, where, they say, 48 per cent of the salaries was for defence and public security, together; of the entire expenditure on salaries in the entire Island, 48 per cent was defence-related. Can you justify that? And I will tell you why that is happening, Sir. On the one hand, you have done nothing to empower the people of the North and the East economically. Despite the fact that in 2009 when the war came to an end, they were 30 years behind economically, you have done nothing to empower them. You did nothing; not only the present Government, but even the 2015 Government did nothing. So, you keep them pauperized, those people become desperate and then, what do you do? Then, your counter-insurgency is to somehow absorb them into your own salary scheme. What salary scheme? Your defence salary scheme. That is happening and it is systematic.\n\nSir, it is for this reason and for all those other reasons that we continue to say that when a force has committed genocide and when we know it, there is no way that we can accept that force to be present at the very least till accountability takes place, till we know that those individuals who are there present in front of us are not criminals so that we know that our children are safe and that they will not get raped like the way they got raped before. That is the reason why we repeatedly say that we want accountability and it will never happen within this country. It will never happen because the system is that, your agenda is that. You need it to carry out your agenda, and it is only through an international mechanism that this situation could be addressed.\n\nFinally, Sir, I am saying - I said it the last time also and I am not saying this to upset people or to make people angry - that the Ministry of Defence is the single most hated Ministry by the Tamil people."
