    "chunk_size_bytes": 1959,
    "chunk_text": "Hon. Member, the second thing you mentioned was about the Rs. 40 profit margin per litre of petrol. There is no Rs. 40 profit margin. I have tabled the profit and loss statement or the cost-reflective pricing formula in Parliament every month after the price revision had been done. Now, the 4 per cent margin accounts to about Rs. 13 to Rs. 14.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0dd9\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dd4\u0dc0 (\u0d85\u0da0\u0dbd\u0daf\u0d9a\u0d9a) \u0dd4\u0dc5\u0dc1\u0d9a\u0dca \u0daf\u0d9d\u0dc0\u0dca\u200d\u0dca \u0daf\u0da2\u0dba \u0d85\u0dcf\u0daf\u0dad\u0dba\u0dd4 \u0dcf\u0daf. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba \u0dc3\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca \u0dbb\u0dcf\u0d9d\u0dc0\u0db1\u0dca \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0b9a\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bb0\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb0\u0bbe\u0b95\u0bb5\u0ba9\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Dr.) Suren Raghavan) Sir, I just want to add to what the Hon. Minister stated. Hon. Dissanayake, since I am in charge of or leading the transformation of higher education, I would like to say that the nuclear scientists in this country are seriously discussing that matter at this point. As you know, the Indian Ocean is a nuclear-free ocean due to the policy that we have had. So, it concerns not only technology, but geopolitics is also involved. Some of our scientists have already been talking to Indian scientists and during the last two visits of the Finance Minister and the Foreign Minister of India, these discussions, not serious but footnote discussions, had taken place. India helped Bangladesh to build a nuclear plant for peaceful energy purposes. So, that is the model our President is also thinking on and we are on that path. Therefore, the Hon. Minister is right on that and from an intellectual point of view or from nuclear scientists\u2019 point of view, we are working on that. Thank you, Hon. Member, for raising that.\n\n543 544\n\n\u0db4\u0daf\u0d9a\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dca \u0dca \u0dd4 \u0dc0\u0dca\u200d"
  },
