    "chunk_text": "Then, there is a delay in completing some projects due to the problem of repaying our internatinal debt. The Kandy-North Pathadumbara Water Supply Project is almost 95 per cent complete. A very small amount has to be paid in order to complete the project, which benefits the electorates of Patha Dumbara, Harispaththuwa, Yatinuwara and many such electorates in the Kandy North area. I think almost 400,000 connections could be given from that. Now, almost everything has been completed and only five per cent needs to be finalized. But, the Chinese Exim Bank has stayed the loan and therefore, the whole project is at a standstill. I think the Hon. Minister needs to talk to the ERD. Of course, we know that this is beyond his control. There is a big problem with regard to Chinese external debt, the Paris Club and their negotiations because they say, \u201cYou have to have equal treatment between the creditors.\u201d With this equal treatment issue, the President and the Finance Ministry are caught up. I hope they would get out of that situation soon. So, these issues should be resolved so that the remaining loan amount could be disbursed to finalize these projects.\n\n673 674\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dca \u0dc4\u0dba \u0dda \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 25\n\nSimilarly, our country is in a situation where we cannot make heavy public investments even on public utilities all the time.\n\nSimilarly, we have several other problems. We have an issue with regard to the Rugam Kithul Reservoir in the Batticaloa District. There was a plan to complete that reservoir, both for irrigation and water supply. The Rugam Kithul Project was proposed in Batticaloa District, but it had not come to total fruition. Also, we have had similar problems in the Northern area, towards Trincomalee. Regarding Yan-Oya, there is a problem. In the Pulmoddai area, with regard to water quality, there is a serious issue. So, we need to look into that and try to improve the water quality in those areas."
