    "chunk_index": 37,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "330d2eed2e32d51d95d0f7924fa2a35c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1917,
    "chunk_text": "Similarly, we have several other problems. We have an issue with regard to the Rugam Kithul Reservoir in the Batticaloa District. There was a plan to complete that reservoir, both for irrigation and water supply. The Rugam Kithul Project was proposed in Batticaloa District, but it had not come to total fruition. Also, we have had similar problems in the Northern area, towards Trincomalee. Regarding Yan-Oya, there is a problem. In the Pulmoddai area, with regard to water quality, there is a serious issue. So, we need to look into that and try to improve the water quality in those areas.\n\nThe other issue is about the Heda Oya Project. The Heda Oya Project is for the benefit of the people of the\n\nPottuvil area. Pottuvil, as you know, Mr. Minister, is a fast-developing tourist area because of the so-called windsurfing facilities available. That is one of the best windsurfing spots in the entire world. Therefore, we get a large number of tourists coming to Pottuvil. But, there is a serious water shortage there. In order to settle the water shortage and to irrigate almost 20,000 acres in that area, increasing the paddy production, that project would be very helpful. We tried to implement the project in the past, but whenever that is being mooted, what happens is, there would always be problems from the farmers in Siyambalanduwa and Pottuvil. There is protest saying that the water is going to be taken away, which should be retained for the people in Siyambalanduwa.\n\nThese are unnecessary political issues. Like how the Kilinochchi farmers had protested against sending water to Jaffna, now the Siyambalanduwa farmers are also taking up that issue in the same way. But, these are all misplaced fears. There is enough water for people both in Siyambalanduwa and Pottuvil. I think we must try to allay the fears of the farmers and the people in the coastal areas of Pottuvil and implement that project."
  },
