    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1704345652008449.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2023-11-25-2023-11-25-0041",
    "chunk_index": 41,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ebc307a2c2f0397ffc03dd6f1dc07714",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1891,
    "chunk_text": "I would just like to address a few of the serious concerns put forward by the Hon. Member. First of all, thank you, Hon. Hakeem, for your kind words, but I am even more indebted for the accusations because they have given me a chance to clarify certain matters.\n\nApart from that, Sir, I would also like to give a few updates. With regard to the pipes you had mentioned, which are are held up in the Harbour and for which we have not paid money, I would like to say that in the third month after my becoming the Minister, we started negotiations with the CICT as well. To be honest, those pipes were bought at Rs. 100-odd million at that point of time, but eventually, it came up to Rs. 1.2 billion with the added demurrages. We were able to negotiate a cut-price on that and right now, all pipes have been taken out, but those have not been distributed yet. There is one issue, the laying of the pipes, regarding which we are talking to the relevant local authorities and we are confident that we would be able to execute that post-Budget.\n\nThere is also one fact that was misrepresented. Over the past 70 years, it is not that we barely reached a coverage of 50 per cent of pipe-borne water connections, but, in fact, 60.4 per cent have been covered by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board alone. Apart from the Water Supply and Drainage Board, we are working, as you said, with the Department of National Community Water Supply. Close to 5,000 Community-Based Organizations - CBOs - are working with us, which is roughly about 15 per cent. So, we have gone further and totally, 95 per cent of the population of the country have access to water now. But, I, as the relevant subject Minister, must admit that there is an issue with the quality of water and also the issue of the local authorities not being equipped to deal with this matter. So, we are coming to a consensus on that."
  },
