    "chunk_size_bytes": 1132,
    "chunk_text": "There is also one fact that was misrepresented. Over the past 70 years, it is not that we barely reached a coverage of 50 per cent of pipe-borne water connections, but, in fact, 60.4 per cent have been covered by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board alone. Apart from the Water Supply and Drainage Board, we are working, as you said, with the Department of National Community Water Supply. Close to 5,000 Community-Based Organizations - CBOs - are working with us, which is roughly about 15 per cent. So, we have gone further and totally, 95 per cent of the population of the country have access to water now. But, I, as the relevant subject Minister, must admit that there is an issue with the quality of water and also the issue of the local authorities not being equipped to deal with this matter. So, we are coming to a consensus on that.\n\n677 678\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbb\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dc6\u0dca \u0dc4\u0dba \u0dda \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2023 \u0dc1\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dc0\u0dd0\u0dda\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 25\n\nCertain water projects which have been stalled, including WaSSIP, the Iranamadu project and other controversial issues, I will be discussing in my speech at the end."
