    "chunk_size_bytes": 2048,
    "chunk_text": "I think what is very important is conservation of water. Sir, I am tabling* this document titled \"Conservation of Water\", a road map on how water needs to be conserved and used efficiently.\n\n823 824\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0dd4\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dad\u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0db1\u0dda \u0dad\u0db6\u0dcf \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0ba8\u0bc2\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bae\u0bb2\u0baf\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Placed in the Library.\n\nI am happy to say that the national average has dropped to 13.5 units per month as opposed to the earlier 15.28 units. Then, I would also like to say that the Integrated Water Resources Management -IWRM- Policy is coming up and that that would solve most of the problems mentioned here in terms of water management.\n\nThen, as regards to the requests made by most of the Members in this House, I think everyone is aware that due to financial constraints, we are not able to take the projects forward. However, we are conducting our donor coordination meetings and are going for a water tariff formula, which will stabilize the water sector and also attract investments. We also need to move forward through public-private partnerships.\n\nSir, there are certain sensitive water projects such as the one in the Matara District, which was brought up by the Hon. Nipuna Ranawaka, the Iranamadu Project referred to by the Hon. Sivagnanam Shritharan and a few other projects. I, as the Minister responsible for those projects, would like to give the assurance that we are going to conduct our mobile visits. In those visits, I will also take part along with my entire team and with public consultation and social feasibility, we will try to finish those projects soon. Even the Hon. Shashindra Rajapaksa brought up the issue of pipes in Monaragala, which project is now at a standstill due to a dispute between the administration and the public. That is not how things should move forward and we are urging for more consultation and cooperation from both sides. So, that is what I would like to say with regard to the National Water Supply and Drainage Board."
