    "md5": "cd84301c54c9a42f241620b26abe4fff",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1559,
    "chunk_text": "Lastly, Sir, I would like to thank my State Minister, who, unfortunately, could not be here due to certain reasons and my officials, especially the Secretary to the Ministry and the heads of institutions. Also, I would like to thank all Members of Parliament and everybody for all their support. Thank you.\n\n\u0dd9\u0db7\u0dcf\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0dd9\u0dba \u0db8\u0dad \u0dad\u0db6\u0db1 \u0dbd\u0daf \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0dc0: \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bc0\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0bae\u0bb5\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f \u0b89\u0bae\u0bb0: Speech tabled:\n\nThe number of community water projects, which were put into implementation throughout the Island in terms of the agreements entered into with the Government of Sri Lanka under the total patronage and financial contribution by organizations such as Asian Development Bank, World Bank, DANIDA and FINNIDA, was nearly 5,000.\n\nNearly 500 of the community water projects started in this way were facing the risk of becoming defunct by 2010. The thenGovernment understood this very well and established the Department of National Community Water Supply for the purpose of arresting the situation and ensuring the sustainability of the community water projects.\n\nAlthough this Department was established in the latter part of the year 2014, the provision allocated for it from the Treasury took a value less than Rs. 100 million due to slow progress in\n\ngetting approval for recruitment schemes necessary to recruit officers necessary for the Department, appointing staffs for it and establishing its Head Office and district offices, which became a strong obstacle for advancing its functions."
  },
