    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "0c3d4bb8bf288e30bb9b5eadd0909e6b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1615,
    "chunk_text": "getting approval for recruitment schemes necessary to recruit officers necessary for the Department, appointing staffs for it and establishing its Head Office and district offices, which became a strong obstacle for advancing its functions.\n\nAs the Department overcame the challenges mentioned above, an annual provision of more than Rs. 1,500 million was allocated every year since 2019 to this Department, which had been moving sluggishly for over five years under an annual provision of Rs. 100 million. It should especially be stated, at a time when action is thus being taken to expand the role of the Department, that the years 2021 and 2022 can be termed years in which the whole world was affected by a gigantic economic crisis. Although, it was possible to control the COVID-19 pandemic to a certain extent, many economies have failed to overcome the economic catastrophes generated by it.\n\nOur economy, which had been stagnant due to the COVID-19 pandemic, saw a further decline in the year 2022 due to global economic trends, especially an economic crisis and the supply of drinking water was also came imperiled as a result. The year 2022 should also be termed the year in which the debt crisis, which had been enveloping our country for a long time, came to a climax.\n\nThe Government has introduced various strategies in order to overcome this economic crisis and owing to the causes such as the country\u2019s political instability and being declared a bankrupt State, the priorities in implementing development activities came under a huge challenge. Annual budgetary provisions were cut by 50 per cent."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
