    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1704345652008449.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2023-11-25-2023-11-25-0273",
    "chunk_index": 273,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7c71ef3b032f131de282a30645bc2a32",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2187,
    "chunk_text": "The Government has introduced various strategies in order to overcome this economic crisis and owing to the causes such as the country\u2019s political instability and being declared a bankrupt State, the priorities in implementing development activities came under a huge challenge. Annual budgetary provisions were cut by 50 per cent.\n\nThe pipe-borne water coverage in Sri Lanka is 59.76 per cent at present and 12.37 per cent is the contribution by the community water projects. More than 722,065 families in over 5,000 villages get their water needs fulfilled through the 4,285 community water projects and it benefits an overall population of over three-and-a-half million.\n\nThe year 2022 goes to history as the period in which the country faced the most challenges and crises. However, it should be noted here that our ability to give water connections to nearly ten thousand families (9,429 to be exact) even amidst such challenges and crises, can be considered a victory that we have achieved.\n\nPresently, the Department of National Community Water Supply is doing a significant role in solving issues related to drinking water and sanitation in rural and estate sector, especially hard to reach areas even to the National Water Supply and Drainage Board, aligning with Sustainable Development Goals.\n\nCurrent involvements:\n\n\uf0b7 Implementation of new water supply schemes for needed\n\npeople under \u201cPraja Jala Abhimani\u201d Programme.\n\n\uf0b7 Rehabilitation and Improvement of existing water supply\n\nschemes.\n\n827 828\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014 * \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0dc0 \u0d85\u0dc0\u0dd9\u0dcf\u0db1\u0db1\u0dda \u0db4 \u0d9a\u0dbb \u0d87\u0dad. * \u0b89\u0bae\u0bb0\u0baf\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bbf\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0baf\u0bbf\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0ba4\u0bb0\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bc1\u0bb3\u0bcd\u0bb3\u0ba4\u0bc1. * Produced at end of speech.\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n\uf0b7 CKDu prevention programme.\n\n\uf0b7 Sanitation Programme.\n\n\uf0b7 Catchment protection programme\n\n\uf0b7 Implementation of Water Safety Plans to mitigate or adaption\n\nto the climate changes. \uf0b7 Implementation of groundwater recharging projects.\n\n\uf0b7 Rainwater harvesting programme\n\n\uf0b7 Strengthening, monitoring and regulating of CBOs for their\n\nsustainability. \uf0b7 Capacity development of Departmental officials."
